  "body": "An open booking time helper could expand a 320px mobile page to 362px and trigger automatic zoom. The fixed-positioning correction prevents that local counterexample. This follow-up corrects a timing error in its regression test: hosted WebKit measurements precede native resize notification by 138\u2013220ms. The added helper assertion demanded an event-driven response before its input arrived.\n\nKeep the immutable first root-overflow and scale checks. Before changing the viewport, arm acknowledgment of a trusted Window resize at the requested dimensions. Require it within the existing eight-second bound, then measure the helper once after the following task permits Popper's queued update. Strict helper edges, content, keyboard focus, root/scale and subsequent scroll tracking remain. Cleanup runs on success and early failure. There is no fit polling, forced update, dismissal, clipping, extra product listener or timeout increase.\n\nThe previous literal pre-notification helper contract remains **FAILED historically**. Its replacement phase is explicit in the contract and supported by the native timelines, [CSSOM View 13.1 (Working Draft)](https://www.w3.org/TR/2025/WD-cssom-view-1-20250916/#resizing-viewports) and [HTML rendering steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#update-the-rendering). These do not prove Popper correctness or a product latency guarantee.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Nine local cases pass with diagnostics; the same nine pass with the observer omitted. Zero skips or retries, against hash-matched unchanged C2 UI artifacts.\n- Three actual controls fail at the intended assertions: removing fixed positioning produces initial 362/320 root overflow; a persistent post-notification helper fault exceeds the edge while the root fits; an untrusted synthetic event cannot satisfy native acknowledgment and the unchanged deadline fails.\n- Repository quality passes with 11 existing platform skips; catalog tests pass 8/8, fresh strict 1,352-candidate audit and specification checks pass. Historical catalog files and all 156 requirement objects remain unchanged. All 1,413 registered source hashes, contract and test are sealed.\n- Independent specification, lifecycle and execution-receipt reviews find no blockers within their scope. Two inherited arithmetic claims and rejecting mutations are rechecked. Browser behavior is **TESTED**, with no new refinement proof; global release assurance remains BLOCKED.\n\nSource: `5cac026c325c7f0ad08b62b08f5ad41b9d0958e7`. Evidence head: `959cf3bc31cc794717e1786b7d133b2907f79322`, following `a9095bc3e3bf53f5a76244564472fe53cfff7691`. [Report and 157 hash-verified artifacts](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/959cf3bc31cc794717e1786b7d133b2907f79322/reports/booking-native-resize-phase-2026-10-29.json) preserve both native failures, controls, source binding, scorecard and limitations. Product UI is unchanged by this follow-up; prior full UI qualification retains its original scope.\n\n[New hosted run](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/40901978115) is pending. The prior run remains 640 passed / three failed / 22 skipped, including separate gallery contrast. Preserve approved #648/#651 for their FIFO slots. Current-head review is requested; all 20 protected checks, strict base, stale-review dismissal, admin/conversation controls and FIFO remain required. Auto-merge is off.\n\nOriginal provider evidence remains unchanged and historical. Separate draft #666 retains its locally verified ticket deadline fix; its hosted backend stops earlier in the existing worker shutdown scenario. No merge, deployment, production financial change or real provider/email operation.",
